        <mxCell id="e100" value="is signed in by" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=0;exitY=0.2;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="session"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e101" value="is Better Auth&apos;s" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="account"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e102" value="is in" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=0;exitY=0.8;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="security_event"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e103" value="signs in with" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="passkey"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e104" value="is sent" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="email_link"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e105" value="is told by" style="edgeStyle=entityRelationEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;startArrow=ERone;startFill=0;endArrow=ERmany;endFill=0;strokeColor=#4a5468;fontColor=#4a5468;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="user" target="email_message"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="n10" value="What someone can reach is user.access, apart from role_id, the capacity they are paid in, which pay rules are written against. Full is everything, and the only level that bills or pays; Field is their own work and what they are paid for it. Someone new starts with Field, and a trigger keeps someone active on Full. Which routes each level reaches is the app&apos;s, in src/lib/access.ts.

Each person keeps a time zone, a locale, a clock and a first day of the week. Empty follows the business&apos;s -- its own timezone and locale -- or what the locale says.

Signing in is with a passkey and nothing else: a key pair made on someone&apos;s phone, computer or security key, of which only the public half is here. There are no passwords. user, session, account and verification are Better Auth&apos;s, in its shape; account can hold no password, and verification keeps the challenge of each passkey being made or signing in until it is answered or lapses.

There is no sign-up: someone with Full adds people on Team, and the first from the command line, and each is emailed a link to make their first passkey. Someone who can&apos;t sign in is sent a link to make a new one, which ends none of theirs. A link also confirms the address someone signs in with, or makes a new one theirs, and using one proves they read mail there: email_verified. An email_link is good once, for an hour at most, and only while it still goes to the address its person signs in with; its code is 256 random bits, of which only the SHA-256 is kept. One of each kind waits at a time, and one used is kept 90 days.

link_try is every code tried that was not one to use, by the network it came from, so a network that keeps trying is turned away, and is kept a day. rate_limit is Better Auth&apos;s count of requests to its own routes, kept here so a restart forgives nothing.

A session is a row, not a stateless token: one server, one database, and every page reads it anyway, so a stateless token would save no round trip and cost revocation. The cookie is the token signed with the server&apos;s secret, so a copy of this table lets nobody in without the secret as well. It lasts until it has gone two weeks unused.

security_event is the security log: every sign-in, refused or not, every passkey and link, everyone added or changed, every change of access and every refusal for lack of it. The database stamps each with its own clock, none is ever changed, and one is removed only once it is a year old. Each person sees their own, and someone with Full everyone&apos;s.

email_message is every email, written in the transaction that makes the change it tells of, so it is sent if and only if that change is kept, and sent afterwards to the relay the environment names. One the relay puts off is tried later each time until send_by; one it refuses for good is given up on. body, and html beside it, are kept only while it is still to send, and a row is deleted after 90 days. Someone is told whenever a passkey of theirs is added or removed, or all of them are ended, and whenever their name, their address or their access changes, or they are made inactive or active again." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#7b8698;whiteSpace=wrap;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="950" width="1540" height="470" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
